    "**Benito Mussolini** took control of the Italian government in 1922.\n\nHe rose to power following the **March on Rome** in October 1922, during which his National Fascist Party organized mass demonstrations to pressure the government. As a result, King Victor Emmanuel III invited Mussolini to form a government, appointing him Prime Minister on October 30, 1922. Over the following few years, Mussolini dismantled democratic institutions to establish a totalitarian dictatorship.",
    "**Benito Mussolini** took control of the Italian government in 1922.\n\nHe rose to power following the **March on Rome** in October 1922, during which his National Fascist Party threatened a coup. To avoid civil war, King Victor Emmanuel III invited Mussolini to form a government, appointing him Prime Minister on October 30, 1922. Over the next few years, Mussolini dismantled democratic institutions to establish a totalitarian dictatorship.",
    "**Benito Mussolini** took control of the Italian government in 1922.\n\nHe rose to power following the **March on Rome** in October 1922, a mass demonstration of his National Fascist Party's paramilitary wing (the \"Blackshirts\"). Fearing civil war, King Victor Emmanuel III invited Mussolini to form a government, appointing him Prime Minister on October 30, 1922. \n\nOver the following few years, Mussolini systematically dismantled democratic institutions to establish a totalitarian dictatorship."
